   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Places in the city and «naar»",
   "texto": [
    "«naar»: «Ga je naar de supermarkt?» (Are you going to the supermarket?), «Ik ga naar het station» (I'm going to the station) is used to indicate movement to a place or city. The city's essential places: «het station» (the train station), «het plein» (the square), «de supermarkt» (the supermarket), «de apotheek» (the pharmacy). To indicate relative location: «naast» (next to), «tegenover» (front of) and «dichtbij» (close to)."
   ]
